30. PVB-011 laws

PVB-011-01 — EXACT REPRESENTATION

Only canonical representations SHALL be signed and verified.

PVB-011-02 — DOMAIN SEPARATION

Signatures SHALL be bound to their protocol/object domain.

PVB-011-03 — KEY BINDING

Signatures SHALL identify the cryptographic key context used for verification.

PVB-011-04 — IDENTITY SEPARATION

Cryptographic identity SHALL remain distinct from presentation.

PVB-011-05 — TEMPORALITY

Signature validity SHALL NOT imply current temporal validity.

PVB-011-06 — PROVENANCE SEPARATION

Signature validity SHALL NOT imply provenance validity.

PVB-011-07 — ANTI-REPLAY

Cryptographic verification SHALL be combined with temporal/contextual replay controls.

PVB-011-08 — KEY ROTATION

Key rotation SHALL preserve reconstructable lineage.

PVB-011-09 — REVOCATION

Revoked keys SHALL NOT silently regain current trust.

PVB-011-10 — AUTHORITY SEPARATION

No cryptographic signature SHALL independently constitute constitutional authorization.

